-- 1903_tx_generic_profile_sourcing_cohort_season2.sql
-- The Texas generic-profile-sourcing cohort. 243 keys written: 173 citation repairs + 70 blanks.
-- 27 further keys are BLOCKED -- all on `immigration`, which has no Season 2 pin -- and 12 are
-- HELD OUT for the operator because their own record proves a rung the chair does not hold.
--
-- 🔴 WHY A FORWARD WRITE. Season 1 is CLOSED and IMMUTABLE. A blank is `value 0` written into
-- the OPEN season, never a DELETE -- a deleted Season 2 row falls back to Season 1 and the bad
-- chair stays visible (CC_0057). Every row written CARRIES THE SOURCES IT EXAMINED.
--
-- ══ WHAT THIS COHORT IS ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- Measured fresh against production: 282 voter-visible keys across 96 Texas state officeholders
-- whose EVERY source is a page about the PERSON -- a capitol.texas.gov member page, a Wikipedia
-- or Ballotpedia biography -- and none of them evidence of a position.
--
-- 🔑 THE MARYLAND RULE GOVERNED THE PASS. A member page LISTS THE MEMBER'S OWN BILLS, so the URL
-- being a profile does not make the row false; in Maryland 70% of the equivalent class carried a
-- verified sponsorship and the fix was a CITATION REPAIR, not retirement (migration 1898). Texas
-- comes out at 71% repairable -- Maryland's number, not Massachusetts's 30%. The class name does
-- not predict the answer; each jurisdiction has to be measured.
--
-- ══ THE EVIDENCE BASE BUILT FOR IT ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- * EVERY MEMBER'S COMPLETE FILED RECORD: 93 members, 1,471 member-session pairs, 81,464 bill
--   entries across author, coauthor, sponsor and cosponsor, EVERY ONE RECONCILED against the
--   count the Texas Legislature Online report prints for itself. 0 count mismatches, 0 errors.
-- * 24 BILLS' ROLL CALLS from the House and Senate Journals, each parsed and checked against the
--   journal's own declared totals.
-- * NINE QUORUM ROLLS from the House Journal, 2021 and 2025. Every one sums to exactly the size
--   of the chamber -- 150 in 2025, 149 in 2021, the latter because Jake Ellzey's seat fell vacant
--   when he won TX-6 that July.
-- * THE TWELVE REDISTRICTING-COMMISSION BILLS these members filed, read for COMPOSITION, which
--   is the only thing that separates rung 1 from rung 2 and which no caption states.
--
-- ══ 🔴🔴 A WRONG-PERSON CONTAMINATION, FOUND BY ACCIDENT AND THEN SWEPT ════════════════════════
-- Ramon Romero Jr. was carried under member code A1390, which the site names TAYLOR REHMET. The
-- code came from the row's OWN CITED URL and was believed without a name check. Because the
-- filed record and the tenure table are both keyed on the code, "his" record was another
-- legislator's: 0 bills and 3 sessions instead of 395 bills and 16. His real code is A3060.
-- 🔑 ALL 93 CODES WERE THEN CHECKED TWO INDEPENDENT WAYS -- against the name report.aspx prints
-- in its header, and against the name MemberInfo.aspx prints -- and the two agreed exactly:
-- 92 confirmed, Romero the only bad one. A confirmer that reuses the generator's predicate is
-- not verification, so neither check reused the way the code was found.
--
-- ══ 🔴🔴 THREE ROWS STATE THE OPPOSITE OF THE RECORD ═══════════════════════════════════════════
-- * Armando Martinez / civil-rights and / trans-athletes: both say he opposed 89(R) SB 12.
--   THE JOURNAL RECORDS A YEA (Record 3506, 88-47). "Martinez Fischer" is printed in full on the
--   same sheet and sits in the ABSENT list, so the bare "Martinez" in the yeas is unambiguous;
--   the roll sums to exactly 150.
-- * Claudia Ordaz / civil-rights: "voted against HB 4040 and SB 12". She is in the SB 12 yeas,
--   and HB 4040 never got a floor vote at all -- it died in Public Education.
-- Each is stated in the repaired row rather than quietly dropped.
--
-- ══ 🔴 A DATED CLAIM THAT DID NOT HAPPEN ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- Armando Martinez / redistricting says he "participated in the quorum break" of 3 August 2025.
-- The House Journal records him PRESENT on all seven 2025 rolls, and on day 5 of the first called
-- session among the members REQUESTING STRICT ENFORCEMENT OF THE CALL -- the motion to compel the
-- absentees back. He did break quorum, in 2021, on both rolls of the second called session.
--
-- ══ 🔴 FOUR ROWS ASSERT A VOTE ON A BILL THAT NEVER GOT ONE ════════════════════════════════════
-- 89(R) HB 44 was left pending in committee; HB 1806 and HB 4040 were referred and never
-- reported. 89(R) SB 16 passed the SENATE 20-11 and then died in the House at Calendars, so for
-- a House member there is no vote on it to have cast.
--
-- ══ 🔴 SEVENTEEN ROWS CITE A MEMBER PAGE THAT DOES NOT EXIST ═══════════════════════════════════
-- Four cited member codes return HTTP 500 in BOTH chambers -- A1290, A1424, A1432, A1442. The
-- real codes are A2150 (Rafael Anchía), A3915 (Ray Lopez), A2365 (Philip Cortez), A3565 (Rhetta
-- Bowers). The citation was to a page that has never existed.
--
-- ══ ⚠ TWELVE ROWS THE NATIONAL DETECTOR COUNTED BY MISTAKE ═════════════════════════════════════
-- "Wikipedia only" treats every en.wikipedia.org URL as a biography. Twelve of these cite an
-- article about the SUBJECT, not the person -- 2025 Texas redistricting (×5), California v. Texas
-- (×2), Operation Lone Star (×2), Texas Senate Bill 4 (2023) (×2), Abbott v. Perez, Moody v.
-- NetChoice. That is evidence of a position, however thin, and inflates the national figure.
--
-- ══ THE VERDICTS ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
--   REPAIRS (173) -- the chair is KEPT and the citation is pointed at the instrument
--      7 PRECISE   the instrument matches ONE rung's text, and only that rung
--    166 BAND      the instrument proves the member's SIDE of the ladder (see below)
--   BLANKS (70)
--     39 NO_INSTRUMENT   party, district, a committee seat or characterisation; nothing to check
--     26 LADDER_SCOPE    the Season 2 rung at this value asks a DIFFERENT QUESTION
--      5 NOT_A_LEGISLATOR  a statewide executive with no member code and so no filed record
--
-- ══ ⚖ BAND versus RUNG -- THE CENTRAL FINDING OF THIS PASS ════════════════════════════════════
-- Texas's record separates the two SIDES of a ladder with certainty and the rungs within a side
-- hardly at all. The 89(2) HB 4 roll call splits this cohort EXACTLY: every chair-1 and chair-2
-- member voted NAY, every chair-4 and chair-5 member voted YEA, 34 of 38 matched. But a quorum
-- break proves opposition to a partisan legislature-drawn map; it cannot choose between an
-- all-citizen commission (1), a party-balanced commission (2) and a supermajority legislative
-- committee (3). A YEA cannot choose between legislative control with court oversight (4) and
-- party control without it (5).
-- Following the operator's Maryland ruling -- a ladder-scope row STAYS until the rescope -- a
-- band-only row is REPAIRED rather than blanked: the chair keeps the placement the original
-- research gave it, and the citation is upgraded from a biography that proves nothing to a dated
-- roll call that proves the side. Each such row says so in its own text.
--
-- ══ 🔑 WHERE THE RECORD *IS* RUNG-PRECISE ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- * trans-athletes rung 4 ("compete only on teams matching their biological sex assigned at
--   birth") IS 87(2) HB 25, captioned "requiring public school students to compete in
--   interscholastic athletic competitions based on biological sex". Same sentence.
--   🔴 AND IT CUTS BOTH WAYS: HB 25 routes transgender students to the team matching their birth
--   sex rather than excluding them from sport, so it does NOT reach rung 5. Two chair-5 rows rest
--   on nothing stronger and are HELD OUT as over-seated, not repaired.
-- * voting-rights rung 5 ("Require documentary proof of citizenship to register to vote") IS
--   89(R) SB 16, word for word.
-- * abortion rung 5 ("ban abortion completely with no exceptions and impose criminal penalties
--   for providers AND PATIENTS") is 89(R) HB 2197 and its companions -- but ONLY THE TEXT SAYS SO.
--   The caption is "protection of an unborn child's rights and criminal liability"; it is
--   SECTION 6, repealing Penal Code §19.06 -- the provision exempting the pregnant woman from
--   prosecution under the homicide chapter -- that makes it rung 5 rather than rung 4.
--
-- ══ ⚠ THREE LADDER MISMATCHES, RECORDED RATHER THAN FORCED ═════════════════════════════════════
-- * religious-freedom. The ladder is entirely about religious EXEMPTIONS from anti-discrimination
--   law. The Texas landmarks are a Ten Commandments display (SB 10) and a school prayer period
--   (SB 11), neither of which creates or limits such an exemption. The members' OWN conscience-
--   protection filings are on the ladder, and those are what the six rows now cite.
-- * climate-change and fossil-fuels both rest on 87(R) SB 13, which bars state investment in
--   companies that boycott energy firms. Neither ladder has a rung about state investment policy.
-- * deportation. Every Texas landmark is about ENFORCEMENT COOPERATION; the ladder asks WHOM to
--   deport. A sheriff-ICE agreement answers no rung on it.
--
-- ══ 🔴 THE CARRY GATE: 88 CHANGED RUNGS, 21 DISTINCT, EACH RULED ON ONCE ════════════════════════
-- A repair keeps the chair, and in Season 2 that is not automatic. 167 of these rows sit on a
-- rung whose text is character-for-character identical. 88 do not; the 21 distinct (topic, rung)
-- pairs were read in both revisions. Sixteen carry -- capitalisation, rewording, or Season 2
-- asking STRICTLY LESS than Season 1 (civil-rights 1 drops "and provide reparations";
-- school-vouchers 1 drops the public-school-funding half and keeps the voucher half the Texas
-- evidence is actually about). Five do not, and those 26 rows are blanked with the finding kept:
--   same-sex-marriage 2 (13 rows) 🔴 THE LADDER WAS RESHUFFLED, NOT REWORDED. Season 1's rung 2 --
--                       "allow same-sex marriage nationwide while protecting some organizations'
--                       right to decline participation" -- is Season 2's rung THREE.
--   voting-rights 2 (8)  ballot ACCESS became VOTER IDENTIFICATION -- the same replacement that
--                       forced 14 ladder-scope blanks in Massachusetts (migration 1900).
--   climate-change 2 (4) SPEED became MECHANISM (ruled the same way in migration 1902).
--   same-sex-marriage 3 (3) a FEDERALISM rung Season 2 does not contain.
--   housing 3 (1)        SUBSIDIES became BINDING RULES; Season 1's rung 3 is Season 2's rung 4.
--
-- ══ ⚠ 12 ROWS HELD OUT FOR THE OPERATOR -- A REPAIR MUST NOT MOVE A CHAIR ══════════════════════
-- These are NOT written here. Each is a row whose own first-person record proves a DIFFERENT rung
-- from the one it sits on, and moving a chair is not a repair:
--   Ann Johnson, Chris Turner / redistricting 1 -> 2. Their own commission bills (HJR 59, HB 241;
--     HJR 83) seat members APPOINTED BY legislators with equal party representation -- rung 2 on
--     any reading. 🔴 Johnson's row says "No specific bill found" while she was the AUTHOR of
--     HB 241 in the very special session she was breaking quorum over.
--   Briscoe Cain, Carrie Isaac / trans-athletes 5 -> 4. Ten and one rung-4 instruments; nothing
--     either filed bans transgender athletes from sport.
--   Ryan Guillen / healthcare 4 -> 2 or 3. 🔴 He AUTHORED TWELVE MEDICAID-EXPANSION BILLS across
--     the 86th and 87th; his row says "No evidence of supporting Medicaid expansion".
--   Chris Turner / fossil-fuels 4 -> 3; Gina Hinojosa / same-sex-marriage 2 -> 1;
--   Juan "Chuy" Hinojosa / same-sex-marriage 3 -> 4 (a 2013 civil-union bill -- a STALE
--     instrument, and the rung fails the carry gate besides).
--   Vikki Goodwin, Penny Morales Shaw, Borris Miles / redistricting -- ⚖ THESE TURN ON A READING
--     OF RUNG 1's OWN WORDS, "no elected officials involved at any level". ALL TWELVE Texas
--     commission bills give elected officials a role: the auditor-draw bills let the four caucus
--     leaders STRIKE eight applicants before the draw, and the agency-draw bills give a
--     four-legislator select committee a veto over the selection pool. Read as "no official
--     SERVES on the commission", Goodwin is right at 1 and Morales Shaw moves 2 -> 1. Read as "no
--     official TOUCHES the process", Morales Shaw is right at 2 and Goodwin moves 1 -> 2. Exactly
--     one of the two is misplaced either way, and the operator decides which.
--   Ken Paxton / redistricting -- NOT IN THE COHORT: his second citation is Abbott v. Perez, the
--     case his own office litigated and won, which is evidence about the position.
--
-- ══ 🔴 27 KEYS CANNOT BE WRITTEN ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
