vil remedy; authorizing discipl" -- filed a conscience-exemption bill, letting a person or facility decline to take part in a service that conflicts with their beliefs; 89(R) HB 2816, as coauthor: "Relating to protection of the rights of conscience of persons from providing and health care facilities from offering certain health care services; pr" -- filed a conscience-exemption bill, letting a person or facility decline to take part in a service that conflicts with their beliefs. ⚠ WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT SETTLE. The instrument places this member firmly on their side of the ladder; it does not by itself separate the rungs WITHIN that side, and the chair keeps the placement the original research gave it. Registered as a ladder-reachability finding rather than silently absorbed.', ARRAY['https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=86R&Bill=HB1035', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=86R&Bill=HB3172', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=86R&Bill=SB1978', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=HB1239', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=HB1424', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=HB525', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=88R&Bill=HB319', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=89R&Bill=HB2816', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/Members/MemberInfo.aspx?Leg=89&Chamber=H&Code=A2825', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steve_Toth']::text[]),
