  -- Tony Tinderholt / religious-freedom  (chair 5 -> 5, REPAIR)
    ('054a67f5-74b5-469b-bba2-0722834bac12'::uuid, '6b9ba6d9-1001-43f5-b073-4d37130696fd'::uuid, '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194'::uuid, 'dfbd847a-294c-49d2-9ac3-69270ea03054'::uuid, 'Citation repaired 2026-10-07 (migration 1903); THE CHAIR IS UNCHANGED. Every source on this row was a page about the person -- a Texas Legislature member page, a Wikipedia or Ballotpedia biography -- and none of them is evidence of a position. They are kept below; the citation now points at what this member actually did. 🔑 THE RECORD: 84(R) HB 3567, as coauthor: "Relating to the rights of certain religious organizations and individuals relating to a marriage that violates a sincerely held religious belief" -- filed a bill exempting officials and organisations from serving a marriage that violates a sincerely held religious belief; 84(R) SB 2065, as cosponsor: "Relating to the rights of certain religious organizations and individuals relating to a marriage that violates a sincerely held religious belief" -- filed a bill exempting officials and organisations from serving a marriage that violates a sincerely held religious belief; 85(R) HB 1805, as coauthor: "Relating to protection of the rights of conscience for child welfare services providers" -- filed a conscience-exemption bill, letting a person or facility decline to take part in a service that conflicts with their beliefs; 85(R) HB 3859, as coauthor: "Relating to protection of the rights of conscience for child welfare services providers" -- filed a conscience-exemption bill, letting a person or facility decline to take part in a service that conflicts with their beliefs; 86(R) HB 1035, as coauthor: "Relating to protecting freedom of conscience from government discrimination" -- filed a conscience-exemption bill, letting a person or facility decline to take part in a service that conflicts with their beliefs; 86(R) HB 3172, as coauthor: "Relating to the protection of membership in and support to religious organizations" -- filed a bill shielding religious organisations from state action; 86(R) SB 1978, as cosponsor: "Relating to the protection of membership in, affiliation with, and support provided to religious organizations" -- filed a bill shielding religious organisations from state action; 87(1) HB 210, as coauthor: "Relating to protection of persons from participation in a health care service for reasons of conscience; providing a civil remedy; authorizing discipl" -- filed a conscience-exemption bill, letting a person or facility decline to take part in a service that conflicts with their beliefs; 87(2) HB 142, as coauthor: "Relating to protection of persons from participation in a health care service for reasons of conscience; providing a civil remedy; authorizing discipl" -- filed a conscience-exemption bill, letting a person or facility decline to take part in a service that conflicts with their beliefs; 87(R) HB 525, as coauthor: "Relating to the protection of religious organizations" -- filed a bill shielding religious organisations from state action; 87(R) HB 1239, as coauthor: "Relating to the prohibited suspension of laws protecting religious freedom and prohibited closure of places of worship" -- filed a bill barring the suspension of religious-freedom protections; 87(R) HB 1424, as coauthor: "Relating to protection of persons from participation in a health care service for reasons of conscience; providing a civil remedy; authorizing discipl" -- filed a conscience-exemption bill, letting a person or facility decline to take part in a service that conflicts with their beliefs; 87(R) HB 1487, as coauthor: "Relating to the protection of religious organizations" -- filed a bill shielding religious organisations from state action; 87(R) HB 3596, as coauthor: "Relating to the protection of religious organizations" -- filed a bill shielding religious organisations from state action; 88(R) HB 319, as coauthor: "Relating to protection of persons from participation in a health care service for reasons of conscience; providing a civil remedy; authorizing discipl" -- filed a conscience-exemption bill, letting a person or facility decline to take part in a service that conflicts with their beliefs. ⚠ WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT SETTLE. The instrument places this member firmly on their side of the ladder; it does not by itself separate the rungs WITHIN that side, and the chair keeps the placement the original research gave it. Registered as a ladder-reachability finding rather than silently absorbed.', ARRAY['https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=84R&Bill=HB3567', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=84R&Bill=SB2065', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=85R&Bill=HB1805', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=85R&Bill=HB3859', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=86R&Bill=HB1035', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=86R&Bill=HB3172', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=86R&Bill=SB1978', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=871&Bill=HB210', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=872&Bill=HB142', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=HB1239', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=HB1424', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=HB1487', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=HB3596', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=HB525', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=88R&Bill=HB319', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tony_Tinderholt']::text[]),
