-- Briscoe Cain / same-sex-marriage  (chair 5 -> 5, REPAIR)
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning = 'Citation repaired 2026-10-07 (migration 1903); THE CHAIR IS UNCHANGED. Every source on this row was a page about the person -- a Texas Legislature member page, a Wikipedia or Ballotpedia biography -- and none of them is evidence of a position. They are kept below; the citation now points at what this member actually did. 🔑 THE RECORD: 85(R) HB 1923, as coauthor: "Relating to the protection of religious beliefs and moral convictions regarding marriage" -- filed a bill protecting refusal to serve a marriage that violates a religious belief; 86(R) HB 4512, as author: "Relating to the rights of persons relating to a marriage that violates a sincerely held religious belief" -- filed a bill protecting refusal to serve a marriage that violates a religious belief. ⚠ WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT SETTLE. The instrument places this member firmly on their side of the ladder; it does not by itself separate the rungs WITHIN that side, and the chair keeps the placement the original research gave it. Registered as a ladder-reachability finding rather than silently absorbed. ⚖ CARRY GATE: the Season 2 text of this rung differs from Season 1 and was read in both revisions -- capitalisation only', sources = ARRAY['https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=85R&Bill=HB1923', 'https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=86R&Bill=HB4512', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Briscoe_Cain']::text[], updated_at = now()
